@startuml
' Figure 12.4  Key per attempt against key per action
' Reading order: top to bottom. Above, the adapter mints a new key for
' each try, so a late credit and the retry are two refunds. Below, the
' key is minted once at the grant, so the retry replays the first.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
participant "Caller" as C <<ops>>
participant "Processor" as P <<ops>>
== Key per attempt (April 14 batch) ==
C -> P : refund, key fw-1
note right of C : 8.0 s, no answer
C -> P : refund, key fw-2
P --> C : credit 1 (late, for fw-1)
P --> C : credit 2 (for fw-2)
note over C, P $F_FAIL : two credits, one refund owed
== Key per action (April 28 path) ==
C -> P : refund, key idem-7f3a
note right of C : 8.0 s, no answer
C -> P : refund, key idem-7f3a
P --> C : credit 1
P --> C : same result, replayed
note over C, P $F_VERIFIED : one credit
@enduml
